>I've recently started playing NetHack and can't decide which character
>class(es) are most likely to do well - my favourites thus far are Samurai
>or Wizards. Has anyone out there got any suggestions/advice?
>Replies via Notes or e-mail welcome!




 ***********SPOILERS TO FOLLOW***********************



























 I think that for the new player the best characters are those that most
easily survive the early levels. In this regard I would suggest that the
Barbarian is by far the easiest character to play since the minimum amount
of subtlety is required. In the early game poison resistance is a vital
intrinsic since one can encounter killer bees or (shudder) soldier ants
in the very early levels (say level 3). Also the Barbarian gets intrinsic
speed at level 7 which is another very important intrinsic for combat. In
addition the hit points on this character seem to go up very quickly with
advancing levels (much more so than a priest, say). The Barbarian also starts
with a two handed sword that can be made into a named weapon. The strength of
this character is also a big plus and his fighting skills are top notch.
I also feel that chaotic is the easiest alignment to have since there are
only 3 named chaotic weapons. It can take forever to get Mjollnir if you're
lawful.

   The priest has some nice features. Especially since he starts with
holy water and often a magic marker. One can easily make blessed scrolls
of enchant weapon or armor. His ability to detect the cursed/blessed state of
objects is nice but not vital.

